#N canvas 0 50 640 460 12;
#X text 20 10 adi-array-proof -- a top-level patch that DECLARES a published array and fills it with a known pattern (ADR-0183).;
#X obj 20 70 adc~ 1 2;
#X obj 20 120 dac~ 1 2;
#X obj 320 60 adi.array \$0 1 8 30 -1 1 - Test;
#X obj 320 130 loadbang;
#X msg 320 180 0 0.125 0.25 0.375 0.5 0.625 0.75 0.875 1;
#X obj 320 240 s \$0-adiarr-1;
#X text 320 290 The \$0 lives in the SEND OBJECT \, not in the message box: \$0 expands in an object box and does NOT expand in a message box \, where it reads as 0. A message box beginning \; \$0-adiarr-1 targets "0-adiarr-1" and Pd reports no such object.;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 1 1 2 1;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
